# One line ending in the repository and in every checkout. Without this a clone
# on a machine whose core.autocrlf=true gets a working copy written in CRLF over
# a tree stored in LF, and git reports every one of those files as modified even
# though no byte of content changed -- which buries the handful that really are.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The shell scripts are entrypoints inside the Linux images; an editor that saves
# CRLF breaks them at exec time, far from the edit that caused it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Converted bytes corrupt these, and the diff of a converted one is unreadable.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.jar binary
observability/jaeger/bin/* binary
